---
source: crates/squawk_linter/src/rules/adding_field_with_default.rs
expression: "lint_errors(sql, Rule::AddingFieldWithDefault)"
---
warning[adding-field-with-default]: adding a column with a volatile default rewrites the table under an `access exclusive` lock
  ╭▸ 
2 │ alter table t add column a float8 default (random());
  │                                           ━━━━━━━━━━
  │
  ├ note: in Postgres 11+, non-volatile defaults can be added without a rewrite
  ╰ help: add the column as nullable, backfill existing rows, and add a trigger to update the column on write instead
warning[adding-field-with-default]: adding a column with a volatile default rewrites the table under an `access exclusive` lock
  ╭▸ 
4 │ alter table t add column b float8 default -random();
  │                                           ━━━━━━━━━
  │
  ├ note: in Postgres 11+, non-volatile defaults can be added without a rewrite
  ╰ help: add the column as nullable, backfill existing rows, and add a trigger to update the column on write instead
